---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PrivacyNotice from '@/components/PrivacyNotice.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config/site';
import { buildSimplePageSchema } from '@/lib/schema';

const description = `Learn how ${siteConfig.name} handles local device-test processing, hosting logs, advertising, cookies, consent choices, analytics, and contact submissions.`;
const jsonLd = buildSimplePageSchema({
  type: 'WebPage',
  name: 'Privacy Policy',
  path: '/privacy-policy/',
  description,
  includePublisher: false,
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />
  <article class="section-sm article-container prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: {siteConfig.updatedDate}</p>
    <PrivacyNotice>
      <strong>Privacy summary:</strong> The device tests perform their primary diagnostic work in
      your browser. Camera video and microphone audio are not uploaded or stored by the testing
      tools. Hosting and the contact-form provider process separate information as described below.
      Advertising, analytics, and a consent platform are disabled at launch.
    </PrivacyNotice>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how {siteConfig.publisherName}, operating {siteConfig.name} at
      {' '}<a href={siteConfig.origin}>{siteConfig.origin}</a>, handles information when you visit the
      website, use browser-based device tests, or contact the publisher.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Website operator</h2>
    <p>
      Publisher: {siteConfig.publisherName}<br />
      Privacy email: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.privacyEmail}`}>{siteConfig.privacyEmail}</a><br />
      General support: <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>
    </p>

    <h2>2. Local device-test processing</h2>
    <p>
      The interactive tests perform their main diagnostic work within the browser. Depending on the
      test, the browser may process camera video, microphone audio, keyboard events, mouse and wheel
      events, touchscreen coordinates, generated audio playback, display-test patterns, browser
      capability information, screen and viewport dimensions, animation-frame timestamps,
      game-controller identifiers and input values, permission states, and a screen-sharing track
      selected by the visitor.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Camera video is displayed locally and is not uploaded, recorded, or stored by the tool.</li>
      <li>
        Microphone audio is analyzed locally and is not uploaded or saved. The microphone tool may
        hold a short sample briefly in volatile memory for optional local playback, then discards it.
      </li>
      <li>Keyboard events are used only while the bounded test is active and are not saved.</li>
      <li>Mouse and touch coordinates remain in the current page session.</li>
      <li>The Dead Pixel Test displays colors and patterns and does not capture the screen.</li>
      <li>
        Screen, viewport, refresh-timing, browser-feature, and controller values are processed only
        in the current browser session and are not uploaded or stored by the tools.
      </li>
      <li>
        The Device Check stops a selected screen-sharing track immediately without preview,
        recording, storage, or upload.
      </li>
      <li>Text results are stored only in temporary in-memory page state.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Browser permissions</h2>
    <p>
      Camera, microphone, fullscreen, and screen-sharing prompts are controlled by the browser or
      operating system. The website requests camera, microphone, or screen access only after a
      deliberate visitor action and a specific explanation. Your browser or operating system may
      remember a decision.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Hosting and security logs</h2>
    <p>
      The website is designed for static hosting. A hosting provider or content-delivery network may
      process IP address, request time, requested URL, user agent, referrer, response status, and
      security or performance logs to deliver and protect the website. The exact provider-side
      retention and processing terms are controlled by the selected host.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Contact messages and FormSubmit</h2>
    <p>
      The Contact page submits information to FormSubmit, a third-party form endpoint that forwards
      messages to {siteConfig.supportEmail}. A submission can include your name, email address,
      selected topic, page URL, browser or device details, message, and acknowledgement. FormSubmit
      and its spam-protection services process this information to deliver the message. FormSubmit
      states that submissions may be retained for 30 days. Your email provider also processes the
      delivered message according to its own terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do not send passwords, authentication codes, payment information, identification documents,
      medical records, confidential workplace material, recordings, private meeting links, or other
      sensitive information.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Advertising is disabled at launch. If Google AdSense is enabled later, Google and advertising
      vendors may process identifiers, device and browser information, IP address, approximate
      location, ad interactions, consent signals, and other information under their own terms. Ads
      must remain manually placed away from active tests and sensitive pages. A Google-certified
      consent platform and accurate vendor disclosure may be required for relevant visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics is disabled at launch. If enabled later, the implementation must not send camera or
      microphone media, key contents, pointer coordinates, touch coordinates, device labels, contact
      text, or detailed diagnostic summaries. Only low-risk events should be considered after privacy
      and legal review.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      The core testing tools do not require cookies, accounts, server sessions, or cloud history. The
      launch build does not set advertising, analytics, or consent storage. FormSubmit may use
      security and anti-spam technology during form submission. Browsers may also store permission
      choices. See the Cookie Policy for more detail.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      Browser test results are not persisted by the tools. They disappear when the page is reloaded,
      closed, or reset. FormSubmit states that form submissions may be retained for 30 days. Messages
      delivered by email may remain in the publisher's mailbox as reasonably needed to respond,
      investigate an issue, maintain records, or protect the website.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not grant a device permission and use the troubleshooting content instead.</li>
      <li>Stop active camera or microphone tracks with the visible control.</li>
      <li>Exit fullscreen or an active input test at any time.</li>
      <li>Do not submit the contact form; use only the public content.</li>
      <li>Use browser settings to clear saved permissions and storage.</li>
      <li>Contact {siteConfig.privacyEmail} with a privacy question or applicable request.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>11. Sensitive use</h2>
    <p>
      The tools are not designed to collect sensitive text, recordings, medical records, financial
      data, or authentication information. Do not type sensitive information in the keyboard test or
      send it through contact channels.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Security</h2>
    <p>
      The project uses static hosting, restrictive headers, no custom backend, and no server-side
      media processing. No website can guarantee absolute security. Browser vulnerabilities,
      malicious extensions, compromised devices, hosting incidents, email compromise, and
      third-party services remain outside the tool's direct control.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated when the publisher, domain, providers, advertising, analytics,
      consent, contact method, retention, legal requirements, or data flow changes. Genuine update
      dates will be used.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
